title: Rifles and Ammunition
subtitle: The fighting groups are short of everything.
view-if: crisis_march = 1 and e21_march_mode = 2
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= Rifles and Ammunition

The fighting groups in the Mansfeld villages have shotguns, a few army rifles from 1918 and almost no ammunition. The miners have dynamite. The police have machine guns and armoured cars. [? if e21_leuna = 0 : Leuna will need every rifle there is. ?]

- @depots: Raid the police depots.
- @miners: Arm the miners with what we have.
- @bury: Bury the rifles for another day.

@depots
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] More rifles for Leuna, and harder blows from the police in Halle.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids armed action.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.red_guards_arms += 10;
RG.district('halle', {repression: 8});
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

A night raid on a police barracks near Eisleben brings in two hundred rifles and a machine gun. Two of our men are killed.

@miners
subtitle: More men in the fight, most of them with pick handles.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('halle', {guards: 3, repression: 4});
Q.e21_ma_out += 20;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Out on strike: about ' + Math.round(Q.e21_ma_out / 10) * 10 + ',000 of the ' + Q.e21_ma_need + ',000 it takes';
Q.crisis_line_2 = ['Leuna: occupied by its workers', 'Leuna: held against the police', 'Leuna: stormed on 29 March', 'Leuna: given up without a fight'][Q.e21_leuna];
Q.crisis_line_3 = (Q.e21_ma_rift >= 5) ? 'At the gates: the other workers have turned on us' : ((Q.e21_ma_rift >= 3) ? 'At the gates: worker against worker' : (Q.e21_ma_rift ? 'At the gates: some fights with the men at work' : 'At the gates: no fights yet'));
!}

The miners' fighting groups double in a day. Half of the new men have nothing but a pick handle.

@bury
subtitle: Some fighters go home. The rifles will still be there when this is over.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_arms_saved = 1;
Q.e21_ma_out = Math.max(20, Q.e21_ma_out - 10);
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Out on strike: about ' + Math.round(Q.e21_ma_out / 10) * 10 + ',000 of the ' + Q.e21_ma_need + ',000 it takes';
Q.crisis_line_2 = ['Leuna: occupied by its workers', 'Leuna: held against the police', 'Leuna: stormed on 29 March', 'Leuna: given up without a fight'][Q.e21_leuna];
Q.crisis_line_3 = (Q.e21_ma_rift >= 5) ? 'At the gates: the other workers have turned on us' : ((Q.e21_ma_rift >= 3) ? 'At the gates: worker against worker' : (Q.e21_ma_rift ? 'At the gates: some fights with the men at work' : 'At the gates: no fights yet'));
!}

The rifles are greased, wrapped in oilcloth and buried in the allotments. The men who bury them are told to forget where.
